From 6068d093abb030521267971781da5b2a6898c319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Young <davidy@funkypenguin.co.nz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:57:35 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: make querying the health index follow contribution,
 under a shared name

The index is built from the NZBs its clients contribute, so reading it and
writing to it are one decision, not two. This was already half true here: the
gated indexer is refused unless BUILTIN_NAB_HEALTH_CONTRIBUTE is on. The
queries were not -- an instance could contribute nothing and still ask the
index about every release it found.

fetchZyclopsHealth now returns no verdicts when not participating, so all
three consequences follow the one decision: no contribution, no queries, no
gated indexer.

Adds ZYCLOPS_INGEST (default true) as a second way to say the same thing.
This is the name shared with the other clients of this index, so one
documented setting means the same thing wherever it is set. Either setting
being false opts out.

Note the consequence for an instance that sets a health API URL without
turning contribution on: its queries now return nothing where before they
were answered. That is the intended reciprocity, and the gated indexer has
always been refused under exactly that condition.

The refusal message names both settings, since either explains it.

TESTS

The rule is expressed as a pure function of the two settings, so it can be
exercised directly -- appConfig is not resolved at module-load time and no
test in this package initialises it. Four tests cover both settings agreeing,
either one opting out, and each default.

Two one-line wrappers that could not be reached by a test were removed rather
than left as uncovered indirection; the three call sites ask the rule
directly.

Mutation-checked: ignoring either setting, and treating an unset contribution
setting as participating, each fail an assertion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
